    "⚠️ A classifier that could not RUN fails the node regardless of that setting." : {
      "comment" : "Warning message for a classifier that could not RUN.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "⚠️ A placeholder that can't be resolved (e.g. a misspelled variable) is left in the output verbatim — check spelling; the validator does not lint Code templates. Never retries; failure routes to the error port." : {
      "comment" : "Warning for a Code node that a placeholder that can't be resolved is left in the output verbatim.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "⚠️ A run executes the last SAVED graph, not your unsaved edits — save before you start one. If you start one anyway, the run says so in its own timeline, so a result that doesn't match your canvas is never a mystery." : {
      "comment" : "A run executes the last SAVED graph, not your unsaved edits.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "⚠️ A scheduled run can never answer a gate, so it ends on the error port either way — wire that port. A timeout does not rescue it; it only delays the same failure, and one longer than the run's overall budget cancels the whole run. See 'Attended vs unattended' below." : {
      "comment" : "Warning for a node that a timeout does not rescue it; it only delays the same failure, and one longer than the run's overall budget cancels the whole run. See 'Attended vs unattended' below.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "⚠️ There is no autosave. Save Changes writes the canvas; Discard Changes throws away everything since the last save — and is itself one Undo away. Unsaved edits survive switching screens and are offered for saving when you quit." : {
      "comment" : "A warning about autosave.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "⚠️ This node's Per-Node Timeout bounds the child's ENTIRE run — size it for the whole child, not one step. Retries share this one ceiling." : {
      "comment" : "Warning for Workflow.Node.Router.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "⚠️ Undo does NOT cover a node's PROFILE — its model, instructions, tools or knowledge. Those are saved to the profile itself, and not only when you press Done: deleting the node, opening another node's inspector, or starting a run — which switches away from the canvas — all save them too. Cancel is the one way to throw them away. The canvas cannot take them back." : {
