    "Match value is required for \"%@\" operator." : {
      "comment" : "A small, red text label below the \"Match value...\" text field, explaining that the \"Match value\" field is required when using a specific condition operator. The placeholder text inside the label is replaced with the name",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Matches the input against labelled rules, top to bottom; each rule's label is an output port. Exactly one match routes there. Anything else — SEVERAL rules matching, or NONE — is decided by one setting, 'When Routing Can't Decide': ask you to pick, route to a rule of your choosing, end the workflow here, or fail onto the error port. Unattended runs (scheduled or chat-bridge) never pause; an Ask uses its 'If nobody can answer' fallback instead. An optional AI Classifier (local MLX model) can name a branch when no pattern rule matched, and its answer follows the same rules — one label routes, none or several fall to the setting." : {

